    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1af73e7a_5c9404a2",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-processes.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 232,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-22T11:26:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Confidentiality (don\u0027t disclose to unauthorized parties) is right, but \"no data … into external tools … or AI-assisted analyzers\" is broader than confidentiality and unenforceable — researchers routinely use scanners/static analyzers, many now AI-backed, and a report from someone who used one but found a real bug is still valuable.\n\nCould we narrow this to non-disclosure (no public trackers / unauthorized sharing) rather than a ban on the reporter\u0027s private tooling?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 231,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 232,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "682f0cb1c0b5f4549564ede893622dfcdc42e949",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dcb1625e_c58abf1a",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-processes.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 243,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-22T11:26:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This \"not accepted\" line (and its twin on 255) is worth reconsidering. A large share of real vulnerabilities are found by reading code, not by weaponizing them — a missing permission check on a REST endpoint is a genuine vuln even without a working exploit. Requiring execution evidence before we\u0027ll even triage risks bouncing legitimate expert reports, whose likely next step is full public disclosure.\n\nCould we soften to \"code-analysis reports are welcome; maintainers may request a PoC when impact is unclear\" rather than a published hard rejection? (Also stated twice — 243 and 255.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 243,
        "startChar": 82,
        "endLine": 243,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "682f0cb1c0b5f4549564ede893622dfcdc42e949",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
